{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1173605-2e-new-wolf-blooded-tells","id":1173605,"title":"[2E] New Wolf Blooded Tells","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-05T15:56:00-08:00","id":1173605,"title":"[2E] New Wolf Blooded Tells","content":"So topic for fan made WB Tells \u2013 share and talk about your own. Here are mine for start\u2026 ( Yes, first one is called <i>exactly</i> like the Facet it\u2019s emulate. )<br /> <br /> <b>Luna\u2019s Embrace</b><br /> Under stress, Wolf-Blooded change his physical sex \u2013 when he rolls Failure on Integrity Breaking Point. The change is biologically complete and functional. The Wolf-Blooded appearance changes so that he or she now looks very much like a twin brother or sister to his or her old self.<br /> <b>Boon:</b> The Wolf-Blooded can will his sex change using his own Willpower. He only need to will it and spend 1 Willpower Point \u2013 he changes sex as Instant Action. Law enforcement are mostly confused when they need to look women instead of men they pursuit before sundown.<br /> <br /> <b>Face in the Water</b><br /> Wolf-Blooded change into Urhan ( or back in to Hishu if being in wolf form already ) when going over running water \u2013 like rivers.<br /> <b>Boon:</b> The Wolf-Blooded change his Forms between Hishu and Urhan each time he is going to get wet more than his one limb or body part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-07-2018, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T17:00:09-08:00","id":1173621,"title":"","content":"I really like this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T17:57:54-08:00","id":1173643,"title":"","content":"There already was a thread for this: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/714377-homebrew-wolf-blooded-tells\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-blooded-tells</a> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1173605-2e-new-wolf-blooded-tells#post1173605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So topic for fan made WB Tells \u2013 share and talk about your own. Here are mine for start\u2026 ( Yes, first one is called <i>exactly</i> like the Facet it\u2019s emulate. )<br /> <br /> <b>Luna\u2019s Embrace</b><br /> Wolf-Blooded change his physical sex each night \u2013 in the moment he sees Moon on the sky. The change is biologically complete and functional. The Wolf-Blooded appearance changes so that he or she now looks very much like a twin brother or sister to his or her old self.<br /> <b>Boon:</b> The Wolf-Blooded can stop the change for one night, using his own Willpower. If he spends 1 Willpower Point when looking on the Moon first time on this night \u2013 he stays in the body from previous 24 hours. With a little devotion, he can stays practically all the time in one sex \u2013 he just need to force his will on each night to not change. Law enforcement are mostly confused when they need to look women instead of men they pursuit before sundown.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Boon isn't really much of one. Nightly changes seem a bit excessive. What about tying it to Breaking Points instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T22:28:11-08:00","id":1173695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1173605-2e-new-wolf-blooded-tells?p=1173643#post1173643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Boon isn't really much of one. Nightly changes seem a bit excessive. What about tying it to Breaking Points instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>So forced changes ( 'curse' part) is on the Breaking Points - and Boon part is based on character Willpower spending and can be multiple times per day, only Willpower Points he needs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T04:35:23-08:00","id":1173731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1173605-2e-new-wolf-blooded-tells?p=1173695#post1173695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So forced changes ( 'curse' part) is on the Breaking Points - and Boon part is based on character Willpower spending and can be multiple times per day, only Willpower Points he needs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that sounds about right. That way the Boon is something you use for your benefit when needed, and the curse us something you have no control over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T06:19:54-08:00","id":1173745,"title":"","content":"Second take on <b>Luna\u2019s Embrace</b> Tell\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Luna\u2019s Embrace</b><br /> Under stress, Wolf-Blooded change his physical sex \u2013 when he rolls Failure on Integrity Breaking Point. The change is biologically complete and functional. The Wolf-Blooded appearance changes so that he or she now looks very much like a twin brother or sister to his or her old self.<br /> <b>Boon:</b> The Wolf-Blooded can will his sex change using his own Willpower. He only need to will it and spend 1 Willpower Point \u2013 he changes sex as Instant Action. Law enforcement are mostly confused when they need to look women instead of men they pursuit before sundown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T22:39:39-08:00","id":1187751,"title":"","content":"Are there any existing tells related to how Werewolves are carnivores? Like something about gaining benefits from eating meat you hunted yourself, but also having a carnivore diet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T23:05:48-08:00","id":1187757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1173605-2e-new-wolf-blooded-tells?p=1187751#post1187751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any existing tells related to how Werewolves are carnivores? Like something about gaining benefits from eating meat you hunted yourself, but also having a carnivore diet?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That's not much of a Tell, though. Link it to 'They can only eat raw meat,' or meat from a carnivore or human, and some benefits would fit. I'd probably have benefits from eating humans be different from just raw meat. Two different Tells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T23:48:01-08:00","id":1187765,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure is carnivore diet should be Tell - Tells are partially benefit. Diet restrictions are only restrictions. It's why they are as <i>drawback</i> in high Primal Urge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T03:33:22-08:00","id":1187791,"title":"","content":"There are already &quot;tracking&quot; Tells so you'd either have to get creative or find another effect for the Boon. Maybe model it like Bone Gnaw - you get information from what you eat?<br /> <br /> For the Drawback, how about using Addicted+Deprived as a model, instead of a hard cap? Or the Sick Condition for non-primarily-meat food?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-20-2018, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T03:36:53-08:00","id":1187795,"title":"","content":"Tells are primarily sell as a problem with side benefits, that was one the most ingenious part of their design that is constantly absent from fan-made ones and is a pity. <br /> <br /> An obligate carnivore Tell that has some benefit is literally they way it should be made. Benefit could be to upgrade the damage of your bite attack if you take out chunks of meat, like werewolves do (normally from Bashing to Lethal, but if you also have the Bite Tell, from Lethal to Aggravated)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T14:45:50-08:00","id":1187982,"title":"","content":"Hm:<br /> <br /> <b>Wolf Spirit</b><br /> <br /> You have some behaviors more akin to a dog than a human; you sniff people upon meeting them, get upset when people enter your personal space without permission, growl when feeling playful or angry, and so on. You need to spend one willpower or roll Resolve + Subterfuge to suppress this for a scene or otherwise subtly downplay it, and many people are put off by it.<br /> <br /> <b>Boon</b>: With a canine mind comes canine empathy. You automatically pick up on what a canid, be they domestic dog, wolf, or even fox, is feeling simply by reading their body language. You can also command all canids with a Presence + Animal Kin roll, though they are bound by their natural behavior and will not put their lives at risk, nor will they go against their training (the guard dog is not going to let you by, though you can confuse him).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T03:40:58-08:00","id":1188122,"title":"","content":"Not bad, I would prefer some minor mechanical tidbit attached to the first part, but that's something everytable can deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T04:48:42-08:00","id":1188130,"title":"","content":"Furry: The Tell?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1173605-2e-new-wolf-blooded-tells?p=1187982#post1187982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm:<br /> <br /> <b>Wolf Spirit</b><br /> <br /> You have some behaviors more akin to a dog than a human; you sniff people upon meeting them, get upset when people enter your personal space without permission, growl when feeling playful or angry, and so on. You need to spend one willpower or roll Resolve + Subterfuge to suppress this for a scene or otherwise subtly downplay it, and many people are put off by it.<br /> <br /> <b>Boon</b>: With a canine mind comes canine empathy. You automatically pick up on what a canid, be they domestic dog, wolf, or even fox, is feeling simply by reading their body language. You can also command all canids with a Presence + Animal Kin roll, though they are bound by their natural behavior and will not put their lives at risk, nor will they go against their training (the guard dog is not going to let you by, though you can confuse him).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T06:08:19-08:00","id":1188155,"title":"","content":"I would say more like otherkin if you really have the need to associate it to a community. That's not what a furry is, as far as I know, wich is not much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T10:10:45-08:00","id":1188208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1173605-2e-new-wolf-blooded-tells?p=1188130#post1188130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furry: The Tell?<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Try Rachel Lindt: The Tell (she's a supevillaness from the web novel Worm, who has the power of Super Dog Training. And ability to mutate them, but she behaves like a sentient version of an abused Rottweiler).<br /> <br /> And yeah, you're thinking otherkin. I was thinking a mechanical widget, but people will react differently to a person who reminds them of a dog, so it seems too varied to model accurately. Generally poorly, but some worse than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T08:35:37-08:00","id":1190284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1173605-2e-new-wolf-blooded-tells#post1173605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So topic for fan made WB Tells \u2013 share and talk about your own. Here are mine for start\u2026 ( Yes, first one is called <i>exactly</i> like the Facet it\u2019s emulate. )<br /> <br /> <b>Luna\u2019s Embrace</b><br /> Under stress, Wolf-Blooded change his physical sex \u2013 when he rolls Failure on Integrity Breaking Point. The change is biologically complete and functional. The Wolf-Blooded appearance changes so that he or she now looks very much like a twin brother or sister to his or her old self.<br /> <b>Boon:</b> The Wolf-Blooded can will his sex change using his own Willpower. He only need to will it and spend 1 Willpower Point \u2013 he changes sex as Instant Action. Law enforcement are mostly confused when they need to look women instead of men they pursuit before sundown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crazy like a Lune. Interesting. So instead of changing into a wolf they just change... into the other gender. Their spirit-connection to Wolf shudders, tries really, really hard to <i>Change</i> and... then says whatever and works with what it has. Cheers mate! Happy conversation with your parents.<br /> <br /> So would a Boon-driven change (as opposed to failing Integrity) create a biologically non-complete and non-functional gender change? In other words, no ability to procreate?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T08:54:40-08:00","id":1190293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1173605-2e-new-wolf-blooded-tells?p=1190284#post1190284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Crazy like a Lune. Interesting. So instead of changing into a wolf they just change... into the other gender. Their spirit-connection to Wolf shudders, tries really, really hard to <i>Change</i> and... then says whatever and works with what it has. Cheers mate! Happy conversation with your parents.<br /> <br /> So would a Boon-driven change (as opposed to failing Integrity) create a biologically non-complete and non-functional gender change? In other words, no ability to procreate?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is pretty much the Wolf Gift Facet, but as a Tell. So the same rules apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T09:45:17-08:00","id":1190312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1173605-2e-new-wolf-blooded-tells?p=1190293#post1190293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is pretty much the Wolf Gift Facet, but as a Tell. So the same rules apply.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ahhhh. Interesting as well. Makes sense then. My knowledge of Gifts is extremely thin, but yes then, reuse rules as often as possible.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T11:01:17-08:00","id":1190342,"title":"","content":"It <i>does</i> raise the question - if one becomes impregnated, and fails a Breaking Point, is it miscarriage or Mr. Seahorse? I suppose, given you can change for 1 Willpower as an instant action, you could just &quot;negate&quot; the change (provided you had Willpower left) and not deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T18:32:12-08:00","id":1190512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1173605-2e-new-wolf-blooded-tells?p=1190342#post1190342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It <i>does</i> raise the question - if one becomes impregnated, and fails a Breaking Point, is it miscarriage or Mr. Seahorse? I suppose, given you can change for 1 Willpower as an instant action, you could just &quot;negate&quot; the change (provided you had Willpower left) and not deal with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consulted the <b>WtF</b> 2E corebook - and agree with your interpretation. Until character has Willpower to spend - I do not see any reason to miscarriage. Because of this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2E, p. 294</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep player agency in mind. Never force a pregnancy on a character unless the player has agreed to it. Likewise, the Storyteller should never bring in any trauma to that character that might result in damage to the fetus or the process of the pregnancy \u2014 unless the player chooses that as the best option. That\u2019s not to say pregnant characters should be immune to <br /> bullets, but rather you should offer Beats or plot hooks in exchange for heightened drama with the pregnancy, and let the player decide how much he or she wants to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were in-depth look in to implications of werewolves pregnancy in <b>Blood of Wolf</b> for 1E - I can look into that for more precise answer if the fetus survive shapechanges on general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}